# Irish Property Reality Check — environment variables
#
# NONE of these are required. The app runs fully with `npm run dev` and zero
# configuration, and so does the one serverless function in api/.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in a value only when you start building the feature it
# belongs to. `.env` is gitignored — never commit real secrets.

# --- Listing metadata (api/listing.ts) ---
# NO KEY REQUIRED, and it should stay that way.
#
# The function reads the Open Graph tags of a single page the user pasted, from a
# hardcoded allowlist of property portals (see api/_lib/urlGuard.ts). Because it
# holds no credentials, compromising it leaks nothing. A managed scraper such as
# Firecrawl was considered and rejected: it would put a per-request cost on the
# app's most-used interaction and would not read anything this does not.

# --- LLM-generated content (future: AI roasts of property descriptions) ---
# Optional. Anthropic API key, used if/when the "AI roast" roadmap item ships.
# Roast the archetype, not the address — mocking a real, named, currently-for-sale
# property carries defamation and estate-agent-complaint risk.
# https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Currency conversion ---
# NO KEY REQUIRED. Rates come from the European Central Bank's free daily feed via
# `npm run ingest:fx`, which regenerates src/data/generated/fx.ts. Paid providers
# (Fixer, Open Exchange Rates) offer nothing extra for euro-base conversion.

# --- Search-backed proof listings (future, Stage 6) ---
# Optional. Whichever provider is chosen; the code is provider-agnostic and
# defaults to a stub. Results are cached per (city, spec-bucket) so cost
# amortises across users rather than scaling per visitor.
SEARCH_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# --- Supabase (future: saved comparisons / shared "misery cards") ---
# Optional. Only needed if a persistence/backend feature is added.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
